    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0472" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1008.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Blanchard.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 31, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 30. When <hi rendition="#italic">Kansas</hi> arrives make similar
                    dispositions for protection of life and property in Gonaives and Saint March
                    that you have for Port au Prince.</p>
                <p>When de facto government is established, Department contemplates conversations
                    looking toward customs convention and a free election under supervision of
                    United States commissioners.</p>
                <p>Continue to keep Department fully advised and include your recommendations,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
